    {
     "tipo": "dialogo",
     "titulo": "Dialogue: raising a public need",
     "frases": [
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "林娜",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       "estudio": "讨论「公民参与」时，社区最需要先了解什么？",
       "alumno": "When discussing «citizen participation», what does the community most need to find out first?",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      },
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "王明",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       "estudio": "我查了几份材料，发现不同来源的说法并不完全一样。",
       "alumno": "I have looked at several materials and found that the sources don't entirely agree.",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      },
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "林娜",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       "estudio": "你打算怎样核实？",
       "alumno": "How do you plan to check it?",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      },
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "王明",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       "estudio": "我会先比较出处，再看论据是否一致。",
       "alumno": "I'll first compare the sources, and then see whether the arguments match.",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      },
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "林娜",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       "estudio": "如果核实后仍有差异呢？",
       "alumno": "What if the differences remain after checking?",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      },
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "王明",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       "estudio": "那就说明不同观点，并把证据的局限写清楚。",
       "alumno": "Then I will set out the different views and make clear the limits of the evidence.",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tipo": "texto",
     "titulo": "Reading: raising a public need",
     "frases": [
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       "estudio": "改善「公民参与」相关的公共服务，首先要了解居民的实际需要。",
       "alumno": "To improve public services related to «citizen participation», first you need to understand residents' real needs.",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      },
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       "estudio": "收集意见之后，应说明如何处理，并让结果可以查询。",
       "alumno": "After collecting opinions, it is advisable to explain how they will be dealt with and to make the results available to check.",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      },
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       "estudio": "如果只凭个人印象，容易忽略其他情况；因此要核对材料，并说明判断依据。",
       "alumno": "If you rely only on personal impressions, you may overlook other cases; that's why you should check the materials and explain the basis for your judgement.",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      },
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       "estudio": "组织短文时，可以先提出观点，再用事实或例子支持它。",
       "alumno": "When organising a short text, you can first put forward a view and then support it with facts or examples.",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
